#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:1
msgid "SDF worlds"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:3
msgid ""
"In this tutorial we will learn how to build our world using SDF, and how to "
"add models to it. Open your text editor and add code as you follow along "
"with this tutorial. You can also download the finished world for this "
"tutorial from [here](https://github.com/gazebosim/docs/blob/master/ionic/"
"tutorials/sdf_worlds/world_demo.sdf)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:5
msgid "Defining a world"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:7
msgid "Every SDF world starts with these tags."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:9
msgid ""
"<?xml version=\"1.0\" ?>\n"
"<sdf version=\"1.8\">\n"
"    <world name=\"world_demo\">\n"
"    ...\n"
"    ...\n"
"    </world>\n"
"</sdf>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:19
msgid ""
"The first two tags define the version of the `XML` and the `SDF`. Then we "
"have the `<world> </world>` tags between which everything goes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:21
msgid "Physics"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:23
msgid ""
"<physics name=\"1ms\" type=\"ignored\">\n"
"    <max_step_size>0.001</max_step_size>\n"
"    <real_time_factor>1.0</real_time_factor>\n"
"</physics>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:30
msgid ""
"The physics tag specifies the type and properties of the dynamic engine. We "
"chose the `name` `1ms` as the step size is 1 millisecond. The `type` is the "
"type of the dynamic engine (physics library). There are options like, Ode, "
"Bullet, Simbody and Dart. We set it to `ignored`, as choosing the type of "
"the physics engine is not done through this tag yet."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:32
msgid ""
"`<max_step_size>` is the maximum time at which every system in simulation "
"can interact with the states of the world. The smaller the value, the more "
"accurate your calculations, but more computation power is needed. "
"`<real_time_factor>` is the ratio of simulation time to real time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:35
msgid "Plugins"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:37
msgid "Plugins are a dynamically loaded chunk of code. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:39
msgid ""
"<plugin\n"
"    filename=\"gz-sim-physics-system\"\n"
"    name=\"gz::sim::systems::Physics\">\n"
"</plugin>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:46
msgid ""
"The `Physics` plugin is very important for simulating the dynamics of the "
"world."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:48
msgid ""
"<plugin\n"
"    filename=\"gz-sim-user-commands-system\"\n"
"    name=\"gz::sim::systems::UserCommands\">\n"
"</plugin>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:55
msgid ""
"The `UserCommands` plugin is responsible for creating models, moving models, "
"deleting them and many other user commands."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:57
msgid ""
"<plugin\n"
"    filename=\"gz-sim-scene-broadcaster-system\"\n"
"    name=\"gz::sim::systems::SceneBroadcaster\">\n"
"</plugin>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:64
msgid "`SceneBroadcaster` shows our world scene."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:66
msgid "GUI"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:68
msgid ""
"Now let's define the GUI. Under the `<gui>` tag we specify anything related "
"to the `GUI` of Gazebo."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:70
msgid ""
"<gui fullscreen=\"0\">\n"
"    ...\n"
"    ...\n"
"</gui>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:77
msgid ""
"[gazebo-gui](https://github.com/gazebosim/gz-gui/) has a bunch of plugins to "
"choose from. We will add the ones that are necessary to get our world up and "
"running with basic functionality."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:79
msgid ""
"<!-- 3D scene -->\n"
"<plugin filename=\"MinimalScene\" name=\"3D View\">\n"
"  <gz-gui>\n"
"    <title>3D View</title>\n"
"    <property type=\"bool\" key=\"showTitleBar\">false</property>\n"
"    <property type=\"string\" key=\"state\">docked</property>\n"
"  </gz-gui>\n"
"\n"
"  <engine>ogre2</engine>\n"
"  <scene>scene</scene>\n"
"  <ambient_light>0.4 0.4 0.4</ambient_light>\n"
"  <background_color>0.8 0.8 0.8</background_color>\n"
"  <camera_pose>-6 0 6 0 0.5 0</camera_pose>\n"
"  <camera_clip>\n"
"    <near>0.25</near>\n"
"    <far>25000</far>\n"
"  </camera_clip>\n"
"</plugin>\n"
"<plugin filename=\"GzSceneManager\" name=\"Scene Manager\">\n"
"  <gz-gui>\n"
"    <property key=\"resizable\" type=\"bool\">false</property>\n"
"    <property key=\"width\" type=\"double\">5</property>\n"
"    <property key=\"height\" type=\"double\">5</property>\n"
"    <property key=\"state\" type=\"string\">floating</property>\n"
"    <property key=\"showTitleBar\" type=\"bool\">false</property>\n"
"  </gz-gui>\n"
"</plugin>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:109
msgid ""
"`MinimalScene` and `GzSceneManager` are responsible for displaying the 3D "
"scene of our world. It has the following properties (most of the GUI plugins "
"have them):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:112
msgid ""
"`showTitleBar` if true it will show the blue title bar over the plugin with "
"the name mentioned in the `<title>` tag."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:113
msgid ""
"`state` is the state of the plugin it can be docked in its place using "
"`docked` or it can be `floating`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:115
msgid ""
"For the rendering engine we can choose `ogre` or `ogre2`. The "
"`<ambient_light>` and the `<background_color>` specify the ambient and the "
"background color of the scene. `<camera_pose>` specifies the `X Y Z` "
"position of the camera followed by its rotation in `Roll Pitch Yaw`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:117
msgid "World control plugin"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:119
msgid ""
"<!-- World control -->\n"
"<plugin filename=\"WorldControl\" name=\"World control\">\n"
"    <gz-gui>\n"
"        <title>World control</title>\n"
"        <property type=\"bool\" key=\"showTitleBar\">false</property>\n"
"        <property type=\"bool\" key=\"resizable\">false</property>\n"
"        <property type=\"double\" key=\"height\">72</property>\n"
"        <property type=\"double\" key=\"width\">121</property>\n"
"        <property type=\"double\" key=\"z\">1</property>\n"
"\n"
"        <property type=\"string\" key=\"state\">floating</property>\n"
"        <anchors target=\"3D View\">\n"
"        <line own=\"left\" target=\"left\"/>\n"
"        <line own=\"bottom\" target=\"bottom\"/>\n"
"        </anchors>\n"
"    </gz-gui>\n"
"\n"
"    <play_pause>true</play_pause>\n"
"    <step>true</step>\n"
"    <start_paused>true</start_paused>\n"
"    <service>/world/world_demo/control</service>\n"
"    <stats_topic>/world/world_demo/stats</stats_topic>\n"
"</plugin>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:145
msgid ""
"The `World control` plugin is responsible for controlling the world. Some of "
"its properties are the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:147
msgid ""
"`<play_pause>` if `true` we will have the play-pause button on the bottom "
"left corner."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:148
msgid ""
"`<stats_topic>` tag specifies the topic at which the world stats like "
"simulation time and real time are published on."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:149
msgid ""
"`<start_paused>` if `true` the simulation will be paused at the start of "
"Gazebo."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:152
msgid "World stats plugin"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:154
msgid ""
"<!-- World statistics -->\n"
"<plugin filename=\"WorldStats\" name=\"World stats\">\n"
"    <gz-gui>\n"
"        <title>World stats</title>\n"
"        <property type=\"bool\" key=\"showTitleBar\">false</property>\n"
"        <property type=\"bool\" key=\"resizable\">false</property>\n"
"        <property type=\"double\" key=\"height\">110</property>\n"
"        <property type=\"double\" key=\"width\">290</property>\n"
"        <property type=\"double\" key=\"z\">1</property>\n"
"\n"
"        <property type=\"string\" key=\"state\">floating</property>\n"
"        <anchors target=\"3D View\">\n"
"        <line own=\"right\" target=\"right\"/>\n"
"        <line own=\"bottom\" target=\"bottom\"/>\n"
"        </anchors>\n"
"    </gz-gui>\n"
"\n"
"    <sim_time>true</sim_time>\n"
"    <real_time>true</real_time>\n"
"    <real_time_factor>true</real_time_factor>\n"
"    <iterations>true</iterations>\n"
"    <topic>/world/world_demo/stats</topic>\n"
"\n"
"</plugin>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:181
msgid ""
"The `World stats` plugin is responsible for displaying the world statistics, "
"`<sim_time>`, `<real_time>`, `<real_time_factor>` and `<iterations>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:184
msgid ""
"With these tags we can choose what values to display (expand the bottom "
"right corner to see these values). We can choose which `<topic>` these "
"values will be published on. Let's try to run the world and listen to that "
"topic."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:186
msgid "Run the world:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:188 ../../../sdf_worlds.md:291
msgid "`gz sim world_demo.sdf`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:190
msgid "Press the play button and in another terminal listen to the messages:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:192
msgid "`gz topic -e -t /world/world_demo/stats`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:194
msgid "The message should look like this:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:196
msgid "![world_shapes_stats](tutorials/sdf_worlds/world_stats.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:196
msgid "world_shapes_stats"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:198
msgid "Entity tree"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:200
msgid ""
"<!-- Entity tree -->\n"
"<plugin filename=\"EntityTree\" name=\"Entity tree\">\n"
"</plugin>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:206
msgid ""
"In this plugin we can see all the entities of our world (everything in "
"simulation is considered an \"entity\"). We can see the different models, "
"sun and also their links, visuals and collisions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:208
msgid "![Entity tree plugin](tutorials/sdf_worlds/entity_tree.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:208
msgid "Entity tree plugin"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:210
msgid "It is blank because we didn't add anything to our world yet."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:212
msgid ""
"There are a bunch of useful gz-gui plugins like the `Transform control` "
"plugin that allows us to manipulate different components of our world, and "
"translate and rotate the entities. Check out this [tutorial]"
"(manipulating_models) explaining how to manipulate models."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:214
msgid ""
"The plugins can also be added from the GUI using the plugin drop-down menu "
"in the top right corner of Gazebo. Now that we are done with the GUI, let's "
"add different elements to our world. **Don't** forget to add the closing tag "
"`</gui>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:216
msgid "Light"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:218
msgid ""
"<light type=\"directional\" name=\"sun\">\n"
"    <cast_shadows>true</cast_shadows>\n"
"    <pose>0 0 10 0 0 0</pose>\n"
"    <diffuse>0.8 0.8 0.8 1</diffuse>\n"
"    <specular>0.2 0.2 0.2 1</specular>\n"
"    <attenuation>\n"
"        <range>1000</range>\n"
"        <constant>0.9</constant>\n"
"        <linear>0.01</linear>\n"
"        <quadratic>0.001</quadratic>\n"
"    </attenuation>\n"
"    <direction>-0.5 0.1 -0.9</direction>\n"
"</light>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:234
msgid ""
"`<light>` specifies the light source in the world. The `<type>` of the light "
"can be `point`, `directional` or `spot`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:235
msgid ""
"`<pose>` is the position (x,y,z) and orientation (roll, pitch, yaw) of the "
"light element with respect to the frame mentioned in the `relative_to "
"attribute`; in our case (`relative_to` attribute is ignored) it is relative "
"to the world."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:236
msgid ""
"`<cast_shadows>` when true the light will cast shadows. `<diffuse>` and "
"`<specular>` are the diffuse and specular light color."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:237
msgid "`<attenuation>` specifies the light attenuation properties, which are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:239
msgid "`<range>` is range of light."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:240
msgid ""
"`<constant>` is the constant attenuation factor, `1` never attenuate and `0` "
"complete attenuation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:241
msgid ""
"`<linear>` is the linear attenuation factor, `1` means attenuate evenly over "
"the distance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:242
msgid ""
"`<quadratic>` is the quadratic attenuation factor. It adds curvature to the "
"attenuation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:243
msgid ""
"`<direction>` is direction of the light, only applicable to spot and "
"directional light."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:245
msgid "Adding models"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:247
msgid ""
"Instead of building our own models we can use already built ones. [Gazebo "
"Fuel](https://app.gazebosim.org/fuel) hosts hundreds of models that can "
"easily be added to an Gazebo world. Models can be added as follows."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:249
msgid "Spawning a model"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:251
msgid ""
"For adding various models from fuel to your world checkout this [tutorial]"
"(fuel_insert)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:253
msgid "Include the model URI"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:255
msgid ""
"Another way of adding the model to your world is to use the model link. "
"Visit the [Gazebo Fuel website](https://app.gazebosim.org/fuel). Choose the "
"model you like and click on the `<>` icon on the model description page. "
"This will copy an SDF snippet to your clipboard, then paste it in your world "
"right above the closing `</world>` tag, like this:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:257
msgid ""
"<include>\n"
"    <uri>\n"
"    https://fuel.gazebosim.org/1.0/OpenRobotics/models/Coke\n"
"    </uri>\n"
"</include>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:265
msgid "Download the model"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:267
msgid ""
"The previous methods download your model on run time. For saving the model "
"permanently you can download the model from fuel, and then refer to it like "
"this:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:269
msgid ""
"<include>\n"
"    <uri>\n"
"    model://Coke\n"
"    </uri>\n"
"</include>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:277
msgid ""
"We need to set `GZ_SIM_RESOURCE_PATH` environment variable to the parent "
"folder of our model. For example, if our directory looks like this:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:279
msgid ""
"world_tutorial<br/>\n"
"├── Coke <br/>\n"
"└── world_demo.sdf\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:285
msgid "Then we have to set it to the `world_tutorial` directory, like this:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:287
msgid "`export GZ_SIM_RESOURCE_PATH=\"$HOME/world_tutorial\"`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:289
msgid "Run your world:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:293
msgid "You should see the model in the origin of the world."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:295
msgid "![world with can](tutorials/sdf_worlds/coke_world.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:295
msgid "world with can"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:297
msgid ""
"You can also set its coordinates using the `<pose>` tag. If you want to "
"spawn multiple instances of the same model you must give them different "
"names with the `<name>` tag."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:300
msgid ""
"    <include>\n"
"        <name>Coke0</name>\n"
"        <pose>0 0 0 0 0 0</pose>\n"
"        <uri>https://fuel.gazebosim.org/1.0/OpenRobotics/models/Coke</uri>\n"
"    </include>\n"
"    <include>\n"
"        <name>Coke1</name>\n"
"        <pose>0 0.1 0 0 0 0</pose>\n"
"        <uri>https://fuel.gazebosim.org/1.0/OpenRobotics/models/Coke</uri>\n"
"    </include>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:312
msgid "![two cans](tutorials/sdf_worlds/two_cokes.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../sdf_worlds.md:312
msgid "two cans"
msgstr ""

